{"author":{"id":"U_kgDOBgAfTQ","is_bot":false,"login":"michael-jong-ds","name":"Michael Jong"},"baseRefName":"master","body":"## 💡 Root Cause <a href=\"#root-cause\" id=\"root-cause\" />\n\n- Empty-state copy (`analytic.no-data-available.description`) hardcoded a mention of \"the tag filter\" even on pages that have no tag filter (Member's Detail Analytics only has a date-range control) → misleading message (#39599).\n- `AnalyticTrendsDateFilter`'s tooltip never surfaced the 31-day custom-range max or the data-retention window, so users hit the limit by trial and error instead of being told upfront (#39602); the component itself was already shared between Workspace Analytics and Member's Detail Analytics, so once traced there was no actual picker-UI divergence to fix, just missing copy.\n- `IAASummaryContent` (Project Report's collapsed IAA table) diverged cosmetically from `IAAContent` (IAA tab / Team Overview's full matrix) — missing the \"Member\" header label and the row bottom-border — which read as an unintentional bug rather than the deliberate reviewer-column omission (#39087).\n- `AnalyticChartWidgetWrapper` watched a form field named `'projectKindField'`, which was never registered anywhere (`AnalyticFilterProvider` registers `'projectKind'`), so project-kind-based `labelType` filtering was a silent no-op on every analytics chart.\n- `AnalyticChartWidgetContent`'s export `useHandler` had a dependency list missing `tagNames`/`chart.name`/`dialog`/`trackEvent` despite using them in the closure — stale-closure risk where an export could use outdated tag filters.\n\n## 🌊 Changes <a href=\"#changes\" id=\"changes\" />\n\n- **Tag-filter-aware empty state (#39599)** — threaded an explicit `hasTagFilter` prop through `AnalyticChartWidget` → context → `AnalyticChart` → `SimpleChartDataQueryHandler` → `ChartDataQueryHandler` → `EmptyAnalyticsData`, so pages without a tag filter (Member's Detail, Project) get \"Try adjusting the date range.\" while Team Overview (which has one) keeps the tag mention. Added `analytic.no-data-available.no-tag-filter.description` i18n key.\n- **Trends limits communicated (#39602)** — extended the shared `AnalyticTrendsDateFilter` tooltip copy to include the 31-day custom-range max and the data-retention window (new `getAnalyticsDataRetentionMonths` helper in `helper.ts`), interpolated via `formatMessage`. Applies to both Workspace Analytics and Member's Detail Analytics since they share the component.\n- **IAA table presentation alignment (#39087)** — `IAASummaryContent.tsx` now renders the same \"Member\" header label and row border as `IAAContent.tsx`; the intentional reviewer-column omission in Project Report is untouched.\n- **Fix dead project-kind filter** — `AnalyticChartWidgetWrapper.tsx` now watches `'projectKind'` instead of the never-registered `'projectKindField'`.\n- **Fix stale-closure export deps** — `AnalyticChartWidgetContent.tsx`'s export handler now depends on the whole (already-memoized) `AnalyticChartWidgetContext` value plus `exportChartFunction`/`dialog`/`trackEvent`, instead of an incomplete hand-picked field list.\n- **De-duplicate chart-grid rendering** — extracted `AnalyticChartsGrid.tsx` to replace three near-identical `loading && data?.result.map(...)` blocks in `TeamMemberAnalyticsPage`, `TeamProjectAnalyticsPage`, and `TeamOverviewWidget`, unifying the loading-spinner UX across all three (previously only the member page showed one).\n- **Empty-check dedup** — extracted `isZeroSum` helper used by `OverallProjectsChart` and `RemainingFilesChart`'s `emptyDataValidator`.\n- **Dead-code removal** — deleted `CheckboxSelectFieldForLabelSet.tsx`, `AnalyticFilterWidget.tsx`/`index.ts`, `AnalyticTrendsFilterWidget.tsx`, and `useGetPaginatedChartDataQuery.ts`/`.gql` — all had zero importers.\n- **UI polish (unrelated pre-existing commit on this branch)** — `EmptyAnalyticsDataMessage.tsx` refactored to `FlexBox`/`Box` layout primitives instead of ad-hoc `styled('div', ...)` wrappers; removed a stale, unused `llm-lab-frontend` i18n key.\n\n## 🧪 How to Test <a href=\"#how-to-test\" id=\"how-to-test\" />\n\n1. Open **Member's Detail Analytics** (Members page → ⋮ → \"View member details\"). With no data in Throughput/Quality, confirm the empty state reads \"Try adjusting the date range.\" (no tag-filter mention).\n2. Open **Team Overview** (Workspace Analytics). Confirm any empty chart still mentions the tag filter, and that hovering the Trends info icon shows both the 31-day max and the data-retention window text.\n3. Open **Member's Detail Analytics** and hover the same Trends info icon — confirm identical tooltip copy/design to step 2.\n4. Open the same project's **Project Report**, **IAA tab** (Project Analytics), and **Team Overview** IAA table side by side — confirm the \"Member\" header label and row borders now match, and Project Report still omits the reviewer-reviewer column.\n5. On any analytics page, apply a project-kind filter (if available) and confirm chart data now actually filters by label type (regression check for the dead-field fix).\n6. Change tag filters on Team Overview, then export a chart — confirm the exported data reflects the current tag filter, not a stale one.\n7. Confirm chart grids on all three pages (Member, Project, Team Overview) show a loading spinner while charts load, and render normally once loaded.\n\n## 🔗 Test Cases <a href=\"#test-cases\" id=\"test-cases\" />\n\n- [QA Test Cases — #39599 Misleading empty state on empty state](https://app.notion.com/p/2ff99635e86682f99b400187236d19d2)\n- [QA Test Cases — #39602 Inconsistent Trends date filter design](https://app.notion.com/p/2e299635e86683bebf7201244cc30833)\n- [QA Test Cases — #39087 Align IAA table presentation](https://app.notion.com/p/dd799635e866832b9f7b0185b3e4bc73)\n\n## 👩‍💻 Implementor's Check list <a href=\"#implementor-check-list\" id=\"implementor-check-list\" />\n\n- [x] **I have performed a self-review from the reviewer's check list and followed all items in the list, and move any inapplicable items to the \"Not Applicable\" bucket at the bottom.**\n  - [ ] I have asked Genie AI to optimize my code changes and apply the recommendations accordingly. [How to use Genie](https://www.notion.so/datasaur/ChatGPT-Genie-AI-299906949201401798c1beb4fd1cce7e)\n  - [ ] I have asked Genie AI to identify potential bugs in my code changes and resolve them accordingly.\n- [x] I have created and filled test cases page for this issue.\n- [ ] I have verified that all test cases written in the [🧪 How to Test](#how-to-test) section are all pass.\n- [ ] A correct number of peer engineers has been assigned.\n  - _Small bug fixes or enhancements must be reviewed by at least 1 peer engineer._\n  - _Significant changes require at least 2 peer engineers._\n    - _**Significant changes**: changes involving more than 10 files or 100 LOC_\n- [ ] A PM/PjM has been assigned to review this PR.\n- [ ] \"Ready\" label is attached to the PR.\n- [ ] Priority label is attached to the PR.\n\n## 🕵️ Reviewer's Check list <a href=\"#reviewer-check-list\" id=\"reviewer-check-list\" />\n\n- [ ] This PR fixed the bug and/or implemented all requirements described in the issue description and/or comments.\n- [ ] The target branch is correct\n  - If specified in the issue description / comments, follow it.\n  - If the issue is labeled as `hotfix`, use the current release branch.\n  - If not specified, the target is master.\n- [ ] The branch name is correct\n  - If this PR is about creating a new feature, the branch name should start with `f/`\n  - If this PR is about enhancing existing features, the branch name should start with `e/`\n  - If this PR is about fixing bugs, the branch name should start with `b/`\n  - If this PR is about fixing bugs and needs to be deployed as hotfix, the branch name should start with `h/`\n  - If this PR is about exploration, the branch name should start with `x/` or `exploration/`\n- [ ] The title of this PR mentioned the issue number being fixed.\n- [ ] The implementor has provided enough information in the description.\n- [ ] Issue(s) being resolved has been connected to this PR.\n\n### Code <a href=\"#code\" id=\"code\" />\n\n- [ ] Changes introduced in this PR are described in [🌊 Changes](#changes) section.\n- [ ] Necessary changes beyond the scope of the issue are listed in [🌊 Changes](#changes) section.\n      _(Example: additional refactor required to implement the task)_\n- [ ] Unnecessary changes beyond the scope of the issue are not committed.\n      _(Example: changes for debugging purpose, i.e: `console.log()`, `debugger;`, setting variables to constants, etc.)_\n- [ ] The code changed in this PR has been covered with tests.\n\n#### Frontend <a href=\"#code-fe\" id=\"code-fe\" />\n\n- [ ] Code changes introduced in this PR followed our [Coding Convention](https://www.notion.so/datasaur/Coding-Conventions-fdecdbc214084d3ca00fe591fe7a9fb0).\n- [ ] GraphQL object or Fragment has `id` or defined data identifiers in [apollo.ts](https://github.com/vulcan-ai/vulcan/blob/master/vulcan-frontend/src/platforms/apollo.ts#L22) ([why?](https://github.com/vulcan-ai/vulcan/pull/16252#issue-1651275934))\n\n##### Event Handler (hover, click, focus, right-click)\n\n- [ ] All handler for menu, buttons, and options **with container** are targeted at container level, not just the inner text. Unless explicitly specified by designer.\n\n##### Context / Provider\n\n- [ ] Component(s) utilizing the relevant context should have Providers mounted as the ancestor component.\n\n## 🔑 GitHub Administrator Notes\n\nIn case of emergency, administrator can bypass branch protections (e.g. merge pull requests without meeting status checks). Please ensure:\n\n- [ ] Provide a reason for bypassing branch protections in the PR for documentation purposes.\n  - During critical situations, for trivial changes (e.g., cosmetic changes, fixing typos), bypass can be performed without providing reasons.\n- [ ] Assign a reviewer to review later after the PR is merged to ensure no misconfiguration, etc.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Not Applicable</summary>\n\n- [ ] TypeORM entities implementing `ListenedEntity` use `repository.save()` to make database changes\n  - `ListenedEntity` uses [`@BeforeInsert()`](https://typeorm.io/listeners-and-subscribers#beforeinsert) and [`@BeforeUpdate()`](https://typeorm.io/listeners-and-subscribers#beforeupdate) decorators from typeorm, which requires `repository.save()` method to be triggered\n\n##### API Guideline <a href=\"#code-be-api-guideline\" id=\"code-be-api-guideline\" />\n\n- [ ] All GraphQL Schemas have been provided with description.\n- [ ] All changes to the GraphQL Schemas have been committed.\n- [ ] All changes to the GraphQL Schemas are backward compatible.\n- [ ] If there any API changes (both breaking or deprecation), please explain the reasons or justifications. Also, provide a customer explanation to handle the changes so that we can copy paste it into this [Release Notes Draft](https://www.notion.so/datasaur/421652d26f2f4da7ba713c6d91eb2872?v=3eef45878fab4c95a2086b495c497d52).\n- [ ] All deletion to the GraphQL Schemas consumed by the frontend are done in separate PRs.\n\n##### API Deprecation\n\n_No API deprecation in this PR._\n\n##### API Breaking Changes\n\n_No API breaking changes in this PR._\n\n###### Migration Guide\n\n_Not applicable._\n\n##### Configuration <a href=\"#code-be-config\" id=\"code-be-config\" />\n\n- [ ] All new configurations have a default value\n- [ ] All dynamic configurations are configurable via environment variables.\n- [ ] New environment variables are documented in these files:\n  - vulcan-backend/.env.example\n  - on-premise/scheme/\\*\\*\\*/build/datasaur.env\n  - on-premise/backend/.env\n\n##### Database <a href=\"#code-be-database\" id=\"code-be-database\" />\n\n- [ ] New unique index are added, before removing the old index. See [incident-38](https://www.notion.so/datasaur/20-February-2025-Production-deployment-failing-due-to-migration-1a099635e86680a7afadcca6e34c1ceb?pvs=4)\n- [ ] Table/Column with important PII or confidential data must be encrypted using AES256Encrypt.\n- [ ] Potentially long running migration has been [rehearsed](https://www.notion.so/Migration-Rehearsal-d493537ee0b04c74ad2f2548c3e6f811).\n- [ ] Table/Column deletion are not committed in the same PR as code deletion. ([why?](https://datasaurlabels.slack.com/archives/CGGKG3CQP/p1672970625753449))\n- [ ] When dropping table or altering field, make sure everything are not broken, e.g. `vulcan-backend`, `seeder`, `glair-agent`.\n- [ ] Glair agent configuration is adjusted if the `label`, `*_answer`, `*_label` tables change.\n- [ ] JSON-type columns are not encrypted\n      If we need a JSON-type column to be encrypted, we should use LONGTEXT as the field type instead. See [this](https://github.com/vulcan-ai/vulcan/issues/18397) for reference\n\n##### Self-hosted Compatibility <a href=\"#code-be-self-hosted\" id=\"code-be-self-hosted\" />\n\n- [ ] New dependencies introduced in Datasaur must also be included in all on-premise scheme. The scheme can be found in on-premise/scheme.\n\n</details>\n\nCloses #39599\nCloses #39602\nRefs #39087\n","files":[{"path":"IAA_V2.4_PLAN.md","additions":0,"deletions":146,"changeType":"DELETED"},{"path":"llm-lab-frontend/src/commons/i18n/messages/en.ts","additions":0,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/app/pages/TeamMemberAnalyticsPage/TeamMemberAnalyticsPage.tsx","additions":13,"deletions":27,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/app/pages/TeamProjectAnalyticsPage/TeamProjectAnalyticsPage.tsx","additions":10,"deletions":40,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/commons/i18n/messages/en.ts","additions":2,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticChartWidget/AnalyticChart.tsx","additions":14,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticChartWidget/AnalyticChartWidget.tsx","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticChartWidget/AnalyticChartWidgetContent.tsx","additions":5,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticChartWidget/AnalyticChartWidgetContext.ts","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticChartWidgetWrapper.tsx","additions":6,"deletions":5,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticChartsGrid.tsx","additions":35,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticFilterWidget/AnalyticFilterWidget.tsx","additions":0,"deletions":29,"changeType":"DELETED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticFilterWidget/index.ts","additions":0,"deletions":1,"changeType":"DELETED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/AnalyticTrendsDateFilter.tsx","additions":45,"deletions":33,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/ChartDataQueryHandler/ChartDataQueryHandler.tsx","additions":9,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/ChartDataQueryHandler/EmptyAnalyticsData.tsx","additions":15,"deletions":10,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/ChartDataQueryHandler/EmptyAnalyticsDataMessage.tsx","additions":11,"deletions":29,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/ChartDataQueryHandler/SimpleChartDataQueryHandler.tsx","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"vulcan-frontend/src/modules/Analytic/components/CheckboxSelectFieldForLabelSet.tsx","additions":0,"deletions":144,"changeType":"DELETED"},{"path":"vulcan-fro